Jean-Yves.Moyen@ens-lyon.org wrote:
> I found a bunch of potion.
> Polypiled them into enlightenment.
> Alchemise them into gain level.
> Use them to get some 40+ great daggers.
> 
> And now, when I throw the great daggers and pick them back, they won't
> stack, thus leading for numerous inventory slot with only " a +0 great
> dagger" although they stack before throwing. And dropping/picking up
> again won't do a thing [moreover i've updated to the version where
> thrown/picked up objects stack correctly].

If you drop some of a stack of daggers, and pick them up, do they restack?


> I know that polypiled object won't stack with regular ones because they
> may unpoypile (this is, by the way, rather anoying when wanting to
> alchemise polypiled potions or mass bless poypiled scrolls). But those
> great daggers did stack before throwing and other objects obtained by the
> same polypile session have turned back to their original form long ago.
> 
> So, bug or feature ?

It sounds logical that each of the daggers could unpolymorph 
independently, so I woud debate that they should stack in the first 
place. The most logical handling of the situation would be for a stack 
of items to still unpolymorph independently, spontaneously splitting off 
from the stack. It is unlikely the game will deal with the situation 
like this though.


> How, by the way. If an item is polypiled into a charged item, used and
> them back to normal. May it be repolypiled into a charged item ?
> 
> More precisely, I had some unihorn in that session. One of them turned
> into a magic marker (1:50 or something like that). I used the marker asap
> (goodbye 'L') and now it's back to a unihorn. Is it possible that this
> horn will again, some day, turn into a charged magic marker ? Won't that
> lead to some kind of polypile abuse ?
> 
I believe that items keep their charge state regardless of whether it's 
used in whatever form the item currently has. So you have a "Unihorn 
(1:infinite)".


